  "summary_en": "1991 European Commission proposal for a Council Directive harmonising medical device regulation under the New Approach. It sets essential requirements, four risk classes, notified-body conformity assessment, CE marking, vigilance on incidents and clinical investigation rules. It predates AI and robotics, and became Directive 93/42/EEC.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Four device classes (I, IIa, IIb, III) set conformity assessment routes by risk",
   "Essential requirements in Annex 1, with presumed compliance via harmonized standards",
   "Notified bodies assess conformity and CE marking is mandatory for market access",
   "Incident vigilance system requires manufacturers to report serious incidents",
   "Clinical investigation rules and safeguard clause allow Member States to restrict risky devices"
